There are 3 things I've noticed about NetHack 3.1.1 that could use some
fixing-up:

1.  The #adjust command doesn't quite work.  I typically play a rogue, who
starts out with around a dozen +0 daggers, in the "b" inventory slot.  Often
I throw these daggers at monsters.  But when I go to pick them up, the
daggers I threw sometimes go to a different inventory letter.  Using the
#adjust command only swaps them instead of merging them.  Then when I drop
those daggers under the other inventory letter and then pick them up again,
they go back to being under the "b" inventory letter.  (Often, but not
always.)

2.  The ^a (repeat) command often doesn't work with the extended commands.
For instance, say I want to #dip my long sword, inventory letter "x", into a
fountain.  I type "#dx".  This dips it once.  But if I use ^a to do it again,
the program assumes that the last thing I typed was "#x", not "#d" or "#dx".

3.  Last night when I was playing, I had a strange experience.  I was in a
shop and picked up a clear potion, which Gomel told me would cost 117 gp.
But when I approached the store exit carrying this unpaid merchandise, Gomel
didn't bother to block the door.  (I wasn't fast and if I waited by the door,
Gomel would block it, then move aside, then block it, etc. as if I wasn't
carrying any unpaid merchandise.)  So I typed "Iu" for an inventory of my
unpaid items, and it gave me an error.  Something to do with a variable 
called cost_something or something_cost.  (Not sure what the something is.)
It also told me that the error had to do with an item (presumably the clear 
potion) being unaccounted for.  It then listed the potion as being unpaid as 
it is supposed to, but then it gave me the message "Program in disorder --
perhaps you'd better Quit."  Well, not wanting to crash the program, I dropped
the potion before leaving the store.  My pet later stole it with no problems
and the program never did crash, but I think it might have had I left the shop
with the unpaid potion.
